From: Rainist7heta <thetamkz621@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:17:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] lcevcdec: report the C++ runtime actually in use

CMakeInstall.cmake probes for libc++ by compiling both branches of an #if,
so the check succeeds regardless of the standard library and the generated
pkg-config file always records -lc++. Debian's clang builds against libstdc++,
where FFmpeg's lcevc_dec >= 4.0.0 probe then fails to link.

Make the non-libc++ branch fail at compile time so the probe reports the
runtime that is actually in use.

---
 cmake/modules/CMakeInstall.cmake | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cmake/modules/CMakeInstall.cmake b/cmake/modules/CMakeInstall.cmake
index 5d7fba1..12fe5a9 100644
--- a/cmake/modules/CMakeInstall.cmake
+++ b/cmake/modules/CMakeInstall.cmake
@@ -43,11 +43,10 @@
             "
         #include <cstddef>
         int main() {
-            #if defined(_LIBCPP_VERSION)
-            return 0;
-            #else
-            return 1;
+            #ifndef _LIBCPP_VERSION
+            #error libc++ is not in use
             #endif
+            return 0;
         }"
             USING_LIBCXX)
 
